{
  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: multimodal, PCA RNA, ViT-L, avgpool, concat → 62.9% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether the RNA modality actually contributes meaningful signal over the image modality alone. Config_009 (image_only, multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool) is a clean ablation: it keeps the image encoder, aggregation, and profile setting identical to config_001 while removing the RNA branch entirely. If image-only performance is close to 62.9%, it suggests PCA-based RNA features add little value and we should redirect budget toward image-side improvements or stronger RNA encoders. If image-only is substantially lower, it confirms multimodal fusion is worthwhile and justifies further investment in optimizing fusion/aggregation. This single experiment resolves the foundational question of whether the multimodal architecture is justified before spending budget on finer-grained fusion or encoder comparisons."
}

